From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0180-texture-mip-trim.patch

Source: 0180-texture-mip-trim.patch
Core patch: goes in tools/eglantine-patches as 0180-... (after 0170). Paths are the submodule's.

The host keeps mip levels from host_level_offset on (TrimmedHostInfo, ImageFlagBits::TrimmedLevels),
until now only for ASTC arrays the GPU decodes whose RGBA8 copy exceeds 1 GiB (Mario Kart World's
8192x8192x68, to 256 MiB on the console). EDEN_NX2_TEX_TRIM_MIB=<MiB> extends the rule, off unless
set: a 2D array of a compressed format (ASTC or BCn; render targets are never compressed) with at
least EDEN_NX2_TEX_TRIM_LAYERS layers (2) whose host copy would take more than the limit keeps one
level less, at most EDEN_NX2_TEX_TRIM_LEVELS (1) below the GPU-decode trim. Host bytes: ASTC as
BC1/BC3 (RGBA8 when not re-compressed), another format at its size.

The upload paths that did not know the offset now drop the copies of levels the host does not
keep before any conversion (ConvertImage and ConvertedLayout take the guest level's size from the
level number) and renumber the rest right before the upload: UploadImageContents (converted and
plain), UploadLayers (plain), QueueAsyncDecode and TickAsyncDecode (both upload paths, the zero
fill too). The GPU-decode path was adapted already; the GPU BCn transcode is not, so arrays it
would take are left alone. Views already map guest to host levels; GPU copies and chunked uploads
already skip trimmed images; the collector counts the host image (0078).

Estimates (the top level is three quarters of a mip chain), with EDEN_NX2_TEX_TRIM_MIB=128:
- Ocarina of Time, 1365x1365x90 x11 levels: 287 MiB (BC3) -> ~72, 152 MiB (BC1) -> ~38:
  about 330 MiB back for the two arrays the refusal reports name.
- Mario Kart World, 8192x8192x68 x12 levels after the GPU-decode trim: 342 -> ~85, 2x94 -> 2x23:
  about 400 MiB. Arithmetic from the refusal reports' sizes, not measured.
Cost: the arrays sample one level blurrier at the nearest distance; a shader that asks for a level
by number gets the one below it. Staging for the whole image is still asked for (MapSizeBytes):
a follow-up could size it from the kept levels. Not compiled, not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
index 27269b5438..c880fb59f6 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
@@ -374,34 +374,109 @@ constexpr std::array<VkFormat, 2> OpaqueAstcViewFormats{VK_FORMAT_BC1_RGBA_UNORM
 // over 1 GiB as RGBA8 (title 1's 8192x8192x68 ASTC 8x8 virtual textures are 24 GB each) keeps only
 // its mip levels from `level_offset` on, so host mip 0 is guest mip `level_offset`. Normalized
 // coordinates and derivative LOD still address it correctly; explicit LODs sample one level lower.
+// EDEN_NX2_TEX_TRIM_MIB=<MiB> (off unless set): a compressed 2D texture array (ASTC or BCn, at
+// least EDEN_NX2_TEX_TRIM_LAYERS layers, default 2) whose host copy would take more than this
+// keeps one level less, at most EDEN_NX2_TEX_TRIM_LEVELS (default 1) below what the rule above
+// already dropped. Its top level is three quarters of the array: Ocarina of Time's 1365x1365x90
+// ASTC arrays hold 287 and 152 MiB as BC3 and BC1 and keep about 72 and 38; Mario Kart World's
+// 8192x8192x68 arrays, 342 and 2x94 MiB after the GPU-decode trim, about 85 and 2x23. Render
+// targets are never compressed, so none is touched. The same TrimmedLevels path as above: views,
+// uploads (UploadImageContents, UploadLayers, the asynchronous decode) and the collector's count
+// follow host_level_offset; a shader that asks for a level by number gets the one below it.
+[[nodiscard]] u64 TextureTrimLimit() {
+    static const u64 limit = [] {
+        const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_TEX_TRIM_MIB");
+        return value != nullptr ? std::strtoull(value, nullptr, 10) << 20 : 0ULL;
+    }();
+    return limit;
+}
+[[nodiscard]] u32 TextureTrimLevels() {
+    static const u32 levels = [] {
+        const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_TEX_TRIM_LEVELS");
+        return value != nullptr ? static_cast<u32>(std::strtoul(value, nullptr, 10)) : 1U;
+    }();
+    return levels;
+}
+[[nodiscard]] u32 TextureTrimLayers() {
+    static const u32 layers = [] {
+        const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_TEX_TRIM_LAYERS");
+        return value != nullptr ? static_cast<u32>(std::strtoul(value, nullptr, 10)) : 2U;
+    }();
+    return layers;
+}
+// The host bytes of `info`'s levels from `skip` on, as the host keeps them: ASTC as BC1 or BC3
+// (RGBA8 when not re-compressed), another format at its own size.
+[[nodiscard]] u64 HostBytesFromLevel(const ImageInfo& info, u32 skip) {
+    u64 numerator = 1, denominator = 1;
+    if (IsPixelFormatASTC(info.format)) {
+        const auto recompression = Settings::GetAstcRecompression();
+        if (recompression == Settings::AstcRecompression::Uncompressed) {
+            numerator = 4;
+        } else if (recompression == Settings::AstcRecompression::Bc1 || info.astc_opaque) {
+            denominator = 2;
+        }
+    } else {
+        numerator = VideoCore::Surface::BytesPerBlock(info.format);
+        denominator = u64{VideoCore::Surface::DefaultBlockWidth(info.format)} *
+                      VideoCore::Surface::DefaultBlockHeight(info.format);
+    }
+    u64 texels = 0;
+    for (s32 level = static_cast<s32>(skip); level < info.resources.levels; ++level) {
+        texels += u64{(std::max)(info.size.width >> level, 1U)} * (std::max)(info.size.height >> level, 1U);
+    }
+    return texels * static_cast<u64>(info.resources.layers) * numerator / denominator;
+}
+
 [[nodiscard]] ImageInfo TrimmedHostInfo(const Device& device, const ImageInfo& info, u32& level_offset) {
     level_offset = 0;
-    if (!WillUseAcceleratedAstcDecode(device, info) || info.type != ImageType::e2D) {
-        return info;
+    const bool decoded_on_gpu = WillUseAcceleratedAstcDecode(device, info) && info.type == ImageType::e2D;
+    if (decoded_on_gpu) {
+        const auto decoded_bytes = [&](u32 skip) {
+            u64 bytes = 0;
+            for (s32 level = static_cast<s32>(skip); level < info.resources.levels; ++level) {
+                bytes += u64{(std::max)(info.size.width >> level, 1U)} *
+                         (std::max)(info.size.height >> level, 1U) * 4;
+            }
+            return bytes * info.resources.layers;
+        };
+        if (decoded_bytes(0) > (u64{1} << 30)) {
+            const u64 limit = TrimmedAstcArrayLimit(device);
+            while (level_offset + 1 < static_cast<u32>(info.resources.levels) &&
+                   decoded_bytes(level_offset) > limit) {
+                ++level_offset;
+            }
+            LOG_WARNING(Render_Vulkan, "{}x{}x{} ASTC image would be {} MiB decoded; keeping mip levels {}+ ({}x{})",
+                        info.size.width, info.size.height, info.resources.layers, decoded_bytes(0) >> 20,
+                        level_offset, (std::max)(info.size.width >> level_offset, 1U),
+                        (std::max)(info.size.height >> level_offset, 1U));
+        }
     }
-    const auto decoded_bytes = [&](u32 skip) {
-        u64 bytes = 0;
-        for (s32 level = static_cast<s32>(skip); level < info.resources.levels; ++level) {
-            bytes += u64{(std::max)(info.size.width >> level, 1U)} *
-                     (std::max)(info.size.height >> level, 1U) * 4;
+    // The opt-in trim: on top of the GPU-decode one, or for an array the CPU converts or uploads as
+    // it is (the GPU BCn transcode's uploads are not adapted to a trim).
+    const u64 trim = TextureTrimLimit();
+    if (trim != 0 && info.type == ImageType::e2D && info.num_samples == 1 &&
+        info.resources.layers >= static_cast<s32>(TextureTrimLayers()) &&
+        (IsPixelFormatASTC(info.format) || IsPixelFormatBCn(info.format)) &&
+        (level_offset != 0 || (!decoded_on_gpu && !WillUseGpuBcnTranscode(device, info)))) {
+        const u32 before = level_offset;
+        while (level_offset - before < TextureTrimLevels() &&
+               level_offset + 1 < static_cast<u32>(info.resources.levels) &&
+               HostBytesFromLevel(info, level_offset) > trim) {
+            ++level_offset;
+        }
+        if (level_offset != before) {
+            LOG_WARNING(Render_Vulkan, "{}x{}x{} array of {} MiB on the host over EDEN_NX2_TEX_TRIM_MIB: keeping mip levels {}+ ({} MiB)",
+                        info.size.width, info.size.height, info.resources.layers, HostBytesFromLevel(info, before) >> 20,
+                        level_offset, HostBytesFromLevel(info, level_offset) >> 20);
         }
-        return bytes * info.resources.layers;
-    };
-    if (decoded_bytes(0) <= (u64{1} << 30)) {
-        return info;
     }
-    const u64 limit = TrimmedAstcArrayLimit(device);
-    while (level_offset + 1 < static_cast<u32>(info.resources.levels) &&
-           decoded_bytes(level_offset) > limit) {
-        ++level_offset;
+    if (level_offset == 0) {
+        return info;
     }
     ImageInfo host = info;
     host.size.width = (std::max)(info.size.width >> level_offset, 1U);
     host.size.height = (std::max)(info.size.height >> level_offset, 1U);
     host.resources.levels -= static_cast<s32>(level_offset);
-    LOG_WARNING(Render_Vulkan, "{}x{}x{} ASTC image would be {} MiB decoded; keeping mip levels {}+ ({}x{})",
-                info.size.width, info.size.height, info.resources.layers, decoded_bytes(0) >> 20,
-                level_offset, host.size.width, host.size.height);
     return host;
 }
 
